{"uid":"242a564750f8c40f","name":"[ELITEA-2017 ELITEA-2058] test_long_response_streams_progressively","fullName":"tests.ui.pipelines.test_pipeline_execution.TestExecutePipelineStreaming#test_long_response_streams_progressively","historyId":"0ba63661d6545751fdcfefa4bd6e6d55","time":{"start":1795842556665,"stop":1795842584784,"duration":28119},"description":"Pipeline with an LLM entry node (TASK F-String ``{input}``)\n        streams a long response progressively, with no console/network\n        errors, and the settled response exceeds 200 characters. Also\n        covers ELITEA-2058 (Model Selector Menu is visible with a\n        non-empty default model before any switch, and the settled\n        response's model-attribution chip proves execution used the\n        model the user selected, not the pipeline's prior default).\n\n        Steps (AFS):\n        1. Pipeline created with LLM entry node, TASK F-String \"{input}\"\n           (fixture — API-created, ready for execution).\n        2. [ELITEA-2058] Verify the Model Selector Menu button is visible\n           and shows a non-empty default model name before any switch.\n           The default is the model the fixture created the pipeline with\n           (``settings.default_model_name`` / ``default_model_display_name``).\n        3. Open the Model Selector Menu, read every listed model and select\n           the one right after the selected (default) one — no hardcoded name.\n        4. Send \"Write a 500-word essay on AI\".\n        5. Verify the response streams progressively (tokens appear\n           incrementally, not all at once).\n        6. Verify the final response is complete and exceeds 200 characters.\n        7. [ELITEA-2058] Verify the settled response's model-attribution\n           chip names the selected model, proving execution\n           used the selected model, not the pipeline's prior default.\n        8. Verify no timeout or error occurs during streaming.\n        ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Pipeline with an LLM entry node (TASK F-String <code>{input}</code>)<br />\nstreams a long response progressively, with no console/network<br />\nerrors, and the settled response exceeds 200 characters. Also<br />\ncovers ELITEA-2058 (Model Selector Menu is visible with a<br />\nnon-empty default model before any switch, and the settled<br />\nresponse's model-attribution chip proves execution used the<br />\nmodel the user selected, not the pipeline's prior default).</p>\n<pre><code>    Steps (AFS):\n    1. Pipeline created with LLM entry node, TASK F-String &quot;{input}&quot;\n       (fixture — API-created, ready for execution).\n    2. [ELITEA-2058] Verify the Model Selector Menu button is visible\n       and shows a non-empty default model name before any switch.\n       The default is the model the fixture created the pipeline with\n       (``settings.default_model_name`` / ``default_model_display_name``).\n    3. Open the Model Selector Menu, read every listed model and select\n       the one right after the selected (default) one — no hardcoded name.\n    4. Send &quot;Write a 500-word essay on AI&quot;.\n    5. Verify the response streams progressively (tokens appear\n       incrementally, not all at once).\n    6. Verify the final response is complete and exceeds 200 characters.\n    7. [ELITEA-2058] Verify the settled response's model-attribution\n       chip names the selected model, proving execution\n       used the selected model, not the pipeline's prior default.\n    8. Verify no timeout or error occurs during streaming.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"browser","time":{"start":1795841596994,"stop":1795841599392,"duration":2398},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestco